  # some code
  # Comment for condition 2
} else if (condition_2) {
  # some code
  # Comment for default
} else {
  # some code
}
```

My first question is whether my original code fits the style people usually follow in R (with or without the empty lines, just for clarity). If the answer is yes, then I guess the formatter is not giving the right output. If the answer is no, how would you write it?

I had a chunk of code I pasted between two `{ }` and expected it to get reindented on save

```r
{
# fmt: skip
fn(
  1
)

fn(
  1
)
}
```

Air gave me:

```r
{
  # fmt: skip
  fn(
  1
)

  fn(
    1
  )
}
```

Interestingly the first line of the `# fmt: skip`'d node gets reindented, but nothing else in the node does

I think this has to do with the fact that the indentation / whitespace before `fn(` is _outside_ of the call node itself, so that indentation gets applied by some standard formatter path. But then it hits `fn(` and refuses to change anything until the end of the node.

Also note that the `# fmt: skip` comment itself also gets reindented, probably by just some standard comment handling.

I'm not entirely sure what result I would expect here, in this particular case I probably wanted

```r
{
  # fmt: skip
  fn(
    1
  )

  fn(
    1
  )
}
```

but I have a feeling that it is not fair of me to ask Air to do that since I marked the node with `# fmt: skip`

