```

~I'd prefer unconditional braces 🤷~ Although I also like the prettier approach where they (mostly) never touch the AST, i.e. they never add in `{` where they are optional https://prettier.io/docs/en/rationale#what-prettier-is-_not_-concerned-about

So the current behavior is probably right, and we would instead have a lint to look for this and suggest a `{` quick fix

I'd be in favour of requiring `{` as soon as the body is pushed to its own line:

```r
function(arg) 1

function(
  arg
) {
  1
}
```

And conversely, always remove the `{` when folding back into one line?
